cup [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* ¼ cup refined rice [[Cookbook:Wine|wine]]\n* 6 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 3 slices of fresh [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 3 dried red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile peppers]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Bring a pot of water to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. Add the quail eggs, and boil for about 10 minutes.\n# Carefully drain the eggs, and cool in cold water.\n# Peel the cooled eggs.\n# Combine the water, soy sauce, sugar, wine, garlic, and ginger in a saucepan. Bring to a boil.\n# Add the eggs to the pot, and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] until the liquid is reduced by half.\n# Add the peppers, and cook just for 1–2 minutes.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Adding 1 tablespoon each of salt and vinegar to the boiling water makes the eggs easier to peel.\n* Don't overcook after adding the chili pepper—it will get too soft.\n\n[[Category:Korean recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using quail egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using soy sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Quail Egg and Chili Jangjorim","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Quail eggs","sourceText":"Quail eggs","amountText":"Quail eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"3 cups water","sourceText":"3 cups water","amountText":"3 cups water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 cup soy sauce","sourceText":"1 cup soy sauce","amountText":"1 cup soy sauce","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ cup sugar","sourceText":"½ cup sugar","amountText":"½ cup sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"¼ cup refined rice wine","sourceText":"¼ cup refined rice wine","amountText":"¼ cup refined rice wine","amount":null,"unit":nu